  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b2171702",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1.2 Splitting training/validation data (fold subsetting)\n",
    "\n",
    "To develop the model, we first need to separate the training and validation data. Independent test data should also be reserved to give an estimate of error for the final model selection."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e4c1e9dc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Scikit-learn has many built-in tools for splitting data that you can explore in [more detail](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/api/sklearn.model_selection.html#splitters) in your own time ([visual examples](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/auto_examples/model_selection/plot_cv_indices.html#sphx-glr-auto-examples-model-selection-plot-cv-indices-py)).\n",
    "\n",
    "For this demo, we use a simple custom class called `CrossValContainer` to keep track of our training and validation data for each fold. \n",
    "We use the sklearn implementation of `KFold` as the simplest random splitter (not recommended for final CV), then introduce two other forms of splitting that are more suitable for geospatial applications: \n",
    "\n",
    "1. by platform: shuffle the data by float WMO, keeping profiles from the same float together during subsetting\n",
    "2. by [k-means clustering](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.cluster.KMeans.html): group the data using spatial coordinates, with optional zonal/meridional weighting\n",
    "\n",
    "All three forms of splitting are called using the `mod_argo` function `subset_folds()`, which helps organize the different types of shuffling into a consistent format. Other splitters (e.g. Leave-One-Out, GroupKFold, RepeatedKFold) can easily be added to the function. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "9a2fb8fc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "/Users/sangminsong/Documents/PROJECTS-PYTHON/BGC-Argo-Workshop-2026/go-bgc-dataworkshop-2026.github.io/book/tutorials/machine-learning/argotools.py:127: UserWarning: you are shuffling a 'ArrowStringArray' object which is not a subclass of 'Sequence'; `shuffle` is not guaranteed to behave correctly. E.g., non-numpy array/tensor objects with view semantics may contain duplicates after shuffling.\n",
      "  ids = platDF[indexer].unique(); np.random.shuffle(ids)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Split data into folds (shuffle by WMO)\n",
    "nfolds = 5\n",
    "cvtainer_bySample = mod_argo.CrossValContainer(trainval_data, nfolds)\n",
    "cvtainer_byProfile = mod_argo.CrossValContainer(trainval_data, nfolds)\n",
    "cvtainer_byKmeans = mod_argo.CrossValContainer(trainval_data, nfolds)\n",
    "\n",
    "# shuffled randomly by sample\n",
    "[cvtainer_bySample.training_inds, \n",
    " cvtainer_bySample.validation_inds] = mod_argo.subset_folds(trainval_data, type='random',\n",
    "                                                            nfolds=nfolds)\n",
    "\n",
    "# by profile (indexer='profid') or by float WMO (indexer='wmoid') \n",
    "[cvtainer_byProfile.training_inds, \n",
    " cvtainer_byProfile.validation_inds] = mod_argo.subset_folds(trainval_data, type='platform',\n",
    "                                                              indexer='profid', \n",
    "                                                              nfolds=nfolds)\n",
    "\n",
    "# by k-means clustering\n",
    "[cvtainer_byKmeans.training_inds, \n",
    " cvtainer_byKmeans.validation_inds] = mod_argo.subset_folds(trainval_data, type='kmeans',\n",
    "                                                            latitude_scaler = 1,\n",
    "                                                            nfolds=nfolds)\n",
    "\n",
    "fold_tags = ['fold' + str(k) for k in range(1, nfolds+1)] # Number of folds"
   ]
  },
